The graph shows a quantity $Q$ modelled by $Q=Ae^{kt}$, with $t$ in years.
Use the $Q$-intercept and the marked point to find $A$ and the exact value of $k$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$t$}, ylabel={$Q$}, xmin=-1, xmax=13, ymin=-10, ymax=95, xtick={5,10}, ytick={40,80}, samples=100, clip=false]
\addplot[thick, ->, domain=0:12] {80*exp(-0.138629*x)};
\addplot[dashed] coordinates {(0,40) (5,40) (5,0)};
\addplot[only marks, mark=*] coordinates {(0,80) (5,40)};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
